# __PROJECT_NAME__

Build with the included Maven Wrapper and JDK 21; no global Maven is required. On PowerShell use `./mvnw.cmd` instead of `./mvnw` and quote `-D...` arguments. Framework artifacts are prepared by the repository Runner; rerun it without `--skipInstall` after changing the framework.
This local game project was generated by zeroServer `scripts/NewLocalGame.java`.

## Three Steps

1. Run the generated smoke once.
2. Open `BUSINESS_GUIDE.md`.
3. Make the first small protocol or business change, then run the test again.

## Run

Use JDK 21+. From the zeroServer repository root, install the framework and run this project with the bundled Maven Wrapper. Replace `path/to/__PROJECT_NAME__` with this project's directory:

~~~powershell
./mvnw.cmd -q -DskipTests install
java scripts/RunLocalScaffold.java --projectDir "path/to/__PROJECT_NAME__"
~~~

On Linux/macOS use `./mvnw` for the install command. No global Maven installation is needed.
If `RunLocalPrototype` just completed successfully, installation, tests and the first run are already done; continue with `BUSINESS_GUIDE.md`.

For later runs from this project directory, the following commands require Maven 3.9+ on PATH. You can also keep using `RunLocalScaffold` from the repository root:

~~~powershell
./mvnw -q clean test
./mvnw -q exec:java
~~~

Expected output:

~~~text
local-game=ok|mode=__RUNTIME_PROFILE__|name=__PROJECT_NAME__|uid=1001|position=3,5|logs=7|metrics=6|maxProtocolId=90202
~~~

