## Boundaries

- This project is a local / prototype scaffold.
- The default selection does not connect external middleware. Adding Redis requires an external service at startup.
- The default demo does not open network ports. Selecting `net` also generates the explicit Server entry described below.
- It does not include account authentication, AOI, broadcast, frame sync, GM security or production deployment config.

## Assembly diagnosis and customization

Run `./mvnw -q -Dexec.mainClass=__PACKAGE__.RuntimeAssembly exec:java` for a read-only diagnosis.
This entry point is available for every template and does not start business services or external clients.
It reports the profile, missing keys, selected providers and schema-declared configuration sources/values.
Sensitive values are masked; complex values are represented by their type. `productionReady=false`.

`RuntimeAssembly.plan(...)` is strict; `RuntimeAssembly.diagnose(...)` returns a shared diagnosis
with an optional plan and a sorted missing-key list. Typed diagnostics cover declared schema keys only.
Use the runtime instance's plan to inspect the configuration actually consumed by that build.

Configuration priority: explicit programmatic/file values > system properties > environment > application defaults
> schema defaults. Standard environment aliases replace dots/hyphens with underscores and use uppercase.
`ZeroConfigLoader.loadStandard(defaults)` only queries keys declared in defaults or the file;
external adapters query their explicitly declared aliases. Invalid higher-priority values fail immediately.

An explicit extension catalog is identified in `zero-scaffold.json` by `catalogId` and `catalogSchemaVersion`.
Use the same trusted `--catalog` file and selected components for subsequent scaffold `--plan`/`--apply` operations.

## Managed local process

From the framework repository root, use scripts/zero.ps1 (PowerShell) or scripts/zero.sh (Bash):

~~~text
run --projectDir "path/to/__PROJECT_NAME__"
serve --projectDir "path/to/__PROJECT_NAME__"
status
stop
~~~

run (alias demo) completes the foreground demo. serve requires the generated local + net Server and waits up to 30 seconds for its ready file; it launches the actual Java process after compilation. --timeoutSeconds accepts 1..60 (stop defaults to 15). State defaults to target/zero-entry; set ZERO_STATE_DIR to isolate multiple projects. Relative paths for process commands resolve from the framework repository root. Use absolute project/config paths for automation.

Server binding accepts only literal 127.0.0.1 or ::1. Set ZERO_NET_PORT=0 for an ephemeral port; explicit Server --host/--port overrides external configuration. The state directory retains per-run stdout/stderr logs. status is an inspection command (zero exit code for idle/exited/not-ready); inspect its zero-status value for health. stop requests cooperative shutdown, waits, and reports forced=true if termination was needed. This development tool does not replace an operating-system service manager.

## Player data and asynchronous responses

LocalGameFixture obtains the `players` repository role from RepositoryCatalog using PlayerProfileRepository.DEFINITION; remote IO belongs to the runtime. The unique selected external data source becomes the default players source; set `zero.player.repositorySource` explicitly when choosing among multiple sources. LocalGameBO implements generated Async interfaces. LocalGameFlow binds generated request/response codecs, and the client decodes real login results. Change Game.si, BO/domain logic and assertions for a new business operation. This loopback prototype has a fixed UID resolver; for verified SecurityContext, request deadlines and durable reward notifications, follow the framework business-slice recipe.
